Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Suggested Experiments", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c8b19ec4-ed9b-f943-ac34-b6809f71d8ee"],

Cell["\<\
1. Observe fourth-order accuracy: In Lab 8A, reduce Slices per Rotor Period \
to 4. Notice how single-step CF4 already beats 4x-more-expensive SubSlices(4) \
while cutting Midpoint error by > 10x.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f389916c-6ecc-0640-87ca-d0ef8721a31f"],

Cell["\<\
2. Rotor-phase collapse: In Lab 8B, set Rotor-Phase Sweep Size = 1 vs 4. A \
single-phase recoupling pulse can easily fail when crystallites start 90 \
degrees or 180 degrees out of phase; sweeping 4 rotor phases forces \
gamma-like robustness.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4f43a0c9-6ff0-9549-b953-01e3e2a190c8"],

Cell["\<\
3. Underpowered recoupling: Drop RF Disk Limit down to 10 kHz at nu_r = 15 \
kHz and observe how Hartmann-Hahn / R-sequence amplitude bottlenecks affect \
recoupling efficiency.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7e29c7d5-660d-5a46-9834-ab47adf371c2"],

Cell["\<\
4. Compare VerifyOptimalControlSimulation under \"Midpoint\" vs \"CF4\" on \
fast spinning rates (15 kHz).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2b8aab03-2aa4-9249-9b77-bfb0fe70ad0e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7b9371c8-2541-f842-8ab1-05b1b9a12c55"],

Cell["\<\
PeriodicFunction combined with fourth-order CF4 DriftIntegration and symbolic \
InitialTimePoint sweeps brings exact-gradient optimal control cleanly to MAS \
solid-state NMR dipolar recoupling, integrating seamlessly downstream with \
NPropagate and periodic Signal1D \"COMPUTE\".\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8b775f24-6f8f-fc4e-be33-775990978883"],

